sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (Nick 2026-11-07): a release stops the slot and rolls it back to its `clean` snapshot. The identity stays. There are no record deletes, no DNS withdrawal, no Metrics membership and no hub peer removal. Enrol: docs/cli/tasks/vm-slot-enrol.mmd; claim: docs/cli/tasks/provision.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · the end of a task group
  %% kind: task_vm.slot_release
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  Note over GW: Release the slot<br/>the group ends
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `tasks:cancel` and `tasks:complete`, as the last child of their run, after approved work is pushed
  %%> - a failed claim
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the intent holds the slot name and its seed clone name
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-slot-release
  SW->>H: Stop the slot<br/>incus stop --force
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops `shark-tvm-3`; a stopped slot counts as done
  SW->>H: Roll back to clean<br/>VM and seed clone
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - restores the `clean` snapshot of the VM and of its seed clone; the task's checkout, containers and files are gone
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - the Node, the WireGuard peer, the identity volume, the agent secret, the Pi token and the model key stay as they are
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>slot clean
    Note over GW: Record the slot free
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the group lets go of the slot; the slot is `free`
    %%> - when the slot's image is not the host's promoted image, the Gateway admits its re-enrol (docs/cli/tasks/vm-slot-enrol.mmd)
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the slot is `failed` and no claim takes it; a new release or a re-enrol repairs it
  end
